# Session-local governance scratch: memory receipts, phase locks, L4 autonomy
# phase/release state, PR handoffs. Carries session identifiers and is rewritten
# per run, so it is never shared branch content. Matches the constellation
# convention (Website-Bot, l9-ci-core, l9-meta-injector, Cognitive.Engine.Graphs).
.l9/

# Governance projections written into this workspace by the Claude Code
# sessionStart bootstrap. Their SSOT is Quantum-L9/Cursor-Governance, which
# tracks all three files; a copy here is a duplicate of another repo's source,
# rewritten on every session. Same reasoning as `.l9/` above.
#
# `.claude/rules` is the sharper case: it is a SYMLINK to an absolute path
# inside the governance clone (`/root/.cursor-governance/...`). Committing it
# would put a machine-specific path in shared branch content and resolve to
# nothing on any other checkout.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `.claude/` — `.claude/hooks/session-start.sh` is
# this repository's own file and stays tracked.
.claude/rules
.claude/settings.json
.claude/hooks/merge_gate_wrap.py
.claude/hooks/session_start_claude_governance.sh

# pnpm's lockfile. This repo's SSOT is package-lock.json (committed, and what
# CI installs with `npm ci`). A second lockfile drifts silently from the first
# and changes what a contributor's install resolves.
pnpm-lock.yaml
